This is a great game, however, there are some pretty bad bugs. The number one problem is the problems with launching the game, which will white screen you tell you that WolfNewOrder or Wolfenstein.exe is not responding. This is easy to fix, (A simple update of AMD Catalyst did it for me. Here's the link to Catalyst 14.4;
) However, users without the know-how to fix the game are basically screwed until Steam releases a patch to fix this huge issue. Other bugs include getting stuck in walls, collision meshes stopping bullets, etc. I myself haven't experienced any FPS drops, except of course when rendering an entire area. Specs; AMD FX-9370 eight core processer, Radeon R7 200 Series, and 8 Gb of ram. Not exactly amazing, but I still play the game on the highest settings with 45-60 FPS.
Now onto the contents of the game;
The story is good, intresting, and sometimes comical when the characters talk. Also, it's quite a challenge. I played on 'Don't hurt me' and still got rekt a bunch of times :D The enemies are intresting, everywhere from Nazi commanders to giant robots and robotic dogs. Awesome gunplay, and if you like to disember Nazi's with a shotgun or blow heads off with a sniper rifle, this is your game! Some say it isn't worth paying $60 for, but honestly if you play it on hard, and look for all the easter eggs and secrets, it's pretty exciting! There's a skill tree you can do challenges to unlock new perks for, and weapon attachments you can find. I recommend the game to anyone who likes to play FPS games like RAGE and Borderlands! However, if you can't fix it manually, it's not worth buying until Steam releases a fix! :D

