I've spent quite some time playing this game... The concept is pretty solid. But only the concept. I've known this game almost from the very beginning and let me tell you a story;
At first, there were only four weapon types: plasma, that fired all at once and then reloaded for some time, SMGs, whose projectiles had no travel velocity (just like CS; if you're in the crossair when i push the mouse button you get instant damage), mediguns who could damage enemies (which was good considering you could only have one weapon type equipped at a time) and snipers that wrecked your♥♥♥♥♥♥up wherever you were. But the max CPU was 1250-something so careful planning and building was important. New cubes were added constantly but the additions were nicely paced so everyone could get used to them. Then the loadout update came and suddenly, all your skills that you got from using your favourite weapon were useless. Then the mech legs came and tank tracks and with them tanks became obsolete. (so long my awesome überdozer...). Then, the mega weapons came (two were avalible long before the LOML (lock-on missile launcher) and others came but were nicely balanced... kind of). Robots started getting copies, the designs were avalible on the "guides" tab but they still somehow ended up more or less unique. During all this, mayor balance changes were made regarding all base weapons, energy came into light. But then, the devs ruined the main part of the game; designing your ultimate robot by inserting the robot factory, where all designs could be sold freely. Great right? Yes, until one thing became clear: the best form of robot  seems to be a so-called "tesseract"; a flying cube with guns sticking out of it. Since then, more and more of those are being used, by the time of me writing this there are at least four per match. Four super fast, super tough and highly damaging opponents. Kinda like tank-scout units with rocket launchers. All other flying units are dying off because of the now overpowered SMGs, everything that cannot lift itself off the ground gets immediately destroyed by plazma, rockets or shotguns, making the wheel as obsolvete as the tank track. To top it off, RNG rewards were implemented and earning currency to get the parts you actually want became tedious and more than anything it consumes time fasten than the cookie monter consumes freshly baked biscuits.
TL;DR: this game is a complete waste of your time. It's like warframe with a ♥♥♥♥♥♥ community.

I used to play planet side outside steam then I decided to include this game here, I'm not a person that plays MMO's mainly because of the pay to play but this game, well this game kills that, having that said alow me to explain.
Pros:
-huge maps, huge community of players;
-be an infantry unit and if you are bored ♥♥♥♥ it, buy a tank or a plane;
-(still on planes) cant shoot♥♥♥♥♥♥ you cant get the hang of it, ♥♥♥♥ it go kamikaze;
-be an insivible sniper that ruins enemy footholds and spots everyone;
-be an annoying light infantry soldier that places c4 explosives while jumping around like Mario with a jet pack;
-be a ♥♥♥♥ing huge infantry soldier enhanced with bazooka and a machine gun, and if you are tired of all the weapons for each class you can unlock more with differet functions, same for vehicles;
-awesome coordination options and leadership perks (I kinda love it the whole place stuff on the map and ask for reinforcements, specially whe  people actually come and you can see your indications being followed and working)
-there's friendly fire and that's +1 point for this game;
-imagine a huge♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥map like huge huge, and the whole map is a pvp area :D with ♥♥♥♥ING HUGE BATTLES WITH AIRCRAFT AND TANKS AND ♥♥♥♥ LOADS OF INFANTRY AND CHARGES AND CRAZY EXPLOSIONS, WITH THE SWEET VICTORY IN THE END WHILE WATCHING THE ENEMIE RETREAT AND GETTING SMASHED WUAHAHAHAHH *heavy breathing* *nerdgasm*
Cons:
-get a good internet connection like really good one;
-I need a new pc, them graphics, check out the youtube videos, really nice graphics;
-sometimes it's a bit unnerving when you get killed over and over again;
-minor glicthes sometimes, and also the lack of unstuck options for vehicles (yeah it happens to me a lot, I know follow the road but big risks big rewards most of the times)
-plane controls are still somewhat ilusive to me but I've been the crew of some nice pilots and they make them work so guess it's about how you do it.
In the end it's an awesome MMO, I have no hacking complains, even if they do I doubt that they will get something out of it the number of stuff happening its just too much they will get killed anyway and as I said this is a massive team game not a solo, impossible in solo mode. And dont worry about pay to play, I have some nice stuff and all for free, takes time I give you that but it's possible to get everything, the only things you actually need to pay are not important (I mean stuff like skins, voice packs, that sort of stuff that lets give tem this guys, they need income in some form)  and they are still developing new features and those features like the "recently added" Valkrie plane are available to all players and that's super nice.
a 10/10
not advisable for:
-if you are a solo player or consider yourself a lone wolf on MMO's this game is not for you, the moment you go to try to steal a base if you are alone is forfeit, just don't;
-it's not about just killing, if you want that this game is not for you, this is about conquering the map and massive team work
